From 6dc9ac2f562f31116183de4846ef4000ff6d6ee1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sidjohn <sidjohn1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:18:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add a replace-device option to reconfigure

Reconfigure now opens a menu: change the device's settings (as before) or replace the
unit with a new one of the same model. A replacement takes over the existing entities and
devices with their entity IDs kept, so history, statistics, dashboards and automations
carry over.

- the new unit must be one that is not set up yet and is the same device class
- it must log in with the entry's own EcoFlow user ID before anything changes
- a backup confirmation is required
- a replacement that keeps the old unit's serial number only changes the address; with a
  new serial the entity unique IDs are rewritten too
- all checks run before any registry change and a failed write is undone
- when no unit matches, the abort message lists why discovered units were skipped

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LkuRKt3ie92aZSAzybLHRy
